  "behavior": [
    "NifSceneTraversal Mode::Full remains default. Selected and Rigid require an explicit live computed NiAVObject mNodeFlags provider, independent of collision flags. Root entry is explicit regardless bit1. A child without bit1 skips the whole subtree. Selected chooses child rigid mode using bit4; Rigid propagates to all entered descendants. Callback updateMode context exposes actual entered mode.",
    "Selected/rigid ordinary node entry always executes own node callbacks. Bit3 gates property callbacks only. Projection bit2 is reinspected after property and own controllers, so controller-driven flag mutations immediately affect world/collision projection. Missing provider or unknown mode rejects before drawing changes; hierarchy/placement/provider/reentrancy guards remain.",
    "Property callbacks can replace the own controller list; inspect the current list after property work, retaining old/current callback leases. Rendering Group/Geode/Drawable scaffolding inherits containing native property policy; preserve OSG drawable callback forms/order and require hierarchy/placement validity afterward.",
    "Skipping projection does not read collision/physics state, settle pending40 or publish a reference. Enabled projection reuses existing native composition/drawing compensation/first-sync/settled writeback and explicit reference migration before children. A missing first-sync handler leaves cached world and pending flags unchanged; retry can complete.",
    "Six tests cover independent properties/own/projection gates, rigid propagation/sibling restoration and foreign visitor context, property/controller-list/child flag mutations, old native child caches/draw worlds, Group/Geode/Drawable policy inheritance, missing/mutating provider/unknown mode rejection, and pending-first-sync/settled physical state gating."
  ],
